  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Satellogic has reached an operational inflection, posting its first positive operating cash flow amid surging demand from defense and sovereign customers. A landmark satellite transfer to a sovereign client and the launch of the Merlin AI-first constellation signal deepening ties to U.S. national security agencies. While geospatial momentum is robust, the stock’s sharp rally has prompted caution that sentiment may have run ahead of near-term fundamentals, creating a tension between strong business execution and stretched positioning.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership has pivoted decisively toward high-value defense work, delivering an in-orbit satellite sale and expanding the Aleph Observer platform. Cost discipline and improved operating leverage have produced early cash generation, boosting credibility with institutional investors now accumulating the stock. Analysts have lifted targets, but the market’s rapid re-rating places a premium on flawless execution and sustained contract wins to justify the elevated optimism.",
